+
+### `truncate_slug(slug, max_length)`
+
+Shortens a slug to at most `max_length` characters. It cuts at the last hyphen that fits, so words are not split, and the result never ends with a hyphen. A single word longer than `max_length` is cut at `max_length`. A `max_length` below 1 raises `ValueError`.
+
+```python
+>>> truncate_slug("hello-world-today", 12)
+'hello-world'
+```
